{"actor":"agent:claude-release-captain","data":{"complexity":"medium","description":"The c11Tests host step in .github/workflows/ci.yml (~line 227) is continue-on-error: true, and main carries 44 pre-existing failing host tests. A new host-test regression therefore never turns CI red. During C11-248 phase 3 the rename orchestrator had to diff the failure list per PR by hand (zero new failures across #482/#483/#484). Fix: triage the 44 (fix, or quarantine with a named skip list and a ticket each), then drop continue-on-error so the step gates. Interim option: a CI step that fails when the failure set grows versus a checked-in baseline. Related: C11-109 (skipped 7 flaky classes), C11-27 (logic/host split).","priority":"high","short_id":"C11-253","status":"backlog","title":"CI: make the c11Tests host step gating again (44 failing tests, regressions invisible)","type":"chore"},"id":"ev_01M3WHCCYSSPQ40643962XG33G","origin":{"op":"task.create","op_id":"op_01M3WHCCYDXF9QZ4JQSVJT09T5","reported":{"branch":"main","client_version":"0.2.1","host":"Hyperion","os_user":"atin","worktree":"/Users/atin/Projects/Stage11/code/c11"}},"schema_version":1,"task_id":"task_01M3WHCCYG828YS5WZ8YM4HB0S","ts":"2026-10-01T20:09:36Z","type":"task_created"}
